From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 99991: steer from the BSS the caller named, not the one we remember

The steer method accepts src_bssid, documents it, and then builds the Client
Steering Request from s->bssid instead - the location this controller has on
record for that client. When that record is stale the request names a BSS the
target agent does not serve, and the agent rejects it.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-03. Client on x8, steered towards 4g:

	ubus call map.controller steer '{... "src_bssid":"00:0c:43:26:60:10" ...}'
	-> {"status":"ok"}

	agent x8: agent_process_steer_request_tlv:
	          Error BSSID 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e not present

7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e is 4g, where the client had been earlier. The controller held
two contradictory records of the same client at that moment:

	sta      7a:6f:6d:db:82:92 -> 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e   (4g, stale)
	sta_mld  7a:6f:6d:db:82:92 -> 00:0c:43:26:60:10   (x8, correct, 33 s old)

so the newer MLD-aware table was right while the legacy one lied, and steering
read the legacy one. The caller had passed the correct source and it was
discarded on the way.

An explicit source is an instruction, not a hint: if the caller names the BSS
the client is on, that is what goes on the wire. Absent one, s->bssid remains
the fallback, unchanged.

Not fixed here, and the larger half of this: when the controller steers on its
own initiative there is no caller to ask, and it will still use s->bssid. The
real repair is for that record to stop going stale - or for this path to prefer
whichever record carries the fresher timestamp. This patch only stops the
controller from overriding an answer it was given.
--- a/src/cntlr_commands_impl.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_commands_impl.c
@@ -1619,13 +1619,36 @@
 	if (!hwaddr_is_zero(target_bssid)) {
 		if (!hwaddr_is_zero(sta)) {
 			struct sta *s = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table, sta);
+			uint8_t explicit_bssid[6] = {0};
+			uint8_t *from_bss;
 
 			if (!s)
 				return -EINVAL;
 
+			/* Where the client is *now*. s->bssid is the record
+			 * held by this controller and can be stale: measured
+			 * 2026-08-03 with the client on x8 while sta.bssid
+			 * still named 4g, which made the agent reject the
+			 * request with "BSSID ... not present" - it was asked
+			 * to steer a client off a BSS it does not serve.
+			 * src_bssid is accepted by this method and was then
+			 * thrown away; an explicit source is an instruction,
+			 * not a hint, so it wins. */
+			from_bss = s->bssid;
+			if (tb[STEER_ATTR_FROM_BSSID]) {
+				char from_bssidstr[18] = {0};
+
+				strncpy(from_bssidstr,
+					blobmsg_data(tb[STEER_ATTR_FROM_BSSID]),
+					sizeof(from_bssidstr) - 1);
+				if (hwaddr_aton(from_bssidstr, explicit_bssid) &&
+				    !hwaddr_is_zero(explicit_bssid))
+					from_bss = explicit_bssid;
+			}
+
 			/* prepare Client Steer Request */
 			cmdu = cntlr_gen_client_steer_request(c, agent,
-							      s->bssid,
+							      from_bss,
 							      steer_op_window,
 							      1, (uint8_t (*)[6])sta,
 							      1, (uint8_t (*)[6])target_bssid,
@@ -1640,7 +1663,7 @@
 			}
 
 			// TODO: unify steer handling
-			cntlr_update_sta_steer_counters(c, s->macaddr, s->bssid,
+			cntlr_update_sta_steer_counters(c, s->macaddr, from_bss,
 							target_bssid, STEER_MODE_BTM_REQ,
 							STEER_REASON_UNDEFINED,
 							255);
